sequenceDiagram
    %% OVIC EON — EON Core 12-Step Initialization Sequence
    %% Document ID: EON-ARCH-DIAG-CORE-INIT-001

    autonumber
    participant Host as OS / Entrypoint
    participant CAM as Core Application Manager
    participant Config as Configuration Manager
    participant Security as Security & Key Manager
    participant Dep as Dependency Resolver
    participant EngReg as Engine Registry
    participant Bus as Core Event Bus
    participant Context as Context Manager
    participant Models as Model Adapter Registry
    participant Health as Health Supervisor

    Host->>CAM: initialize()
    CAM->>Config: Step 1: Load & validate configuration
    Config-->>CAM: Configuration OK
    CAM->>CAM: Step 2: Validate OS environment (RAM/CPU/Python)
    CAM->>Security: Step 3: Initialize CryptoShredder & Key Store
    Security-->>CAM: Keys OK
    CAM->>Dep: Step 4: Build dependency graph & check DAG
    Dep-->>CAM: Acyclic Graph Verified
    CAM->>CAM: Step 5: Register Core singleton services
    CAM->>EngReg: Step 6: Discover & register seven engines
    EngReg-->>CAM: 7 Engines Registered
    CAM->>CAM: Step 7: Verify engine interface contracts
    CAM->>Context: Step 8: Initialize SessionContext & WorkingMemory
    Context-->>CAM: Context Ready
    CAM->>Bus: Step 9: Start EventBus router & bounded queues
    Bus-->>CAM: Event Bus Running
    CAM->>Models: Step 10: Detect hardware & register local adapters
    Models-->>CAM: Models Cataloged
    CAM->>Health: Step 11: Execute pre-flight subsystem health check
    Health-->>CAM: System All Green
    CAM->>Host: Step 12: Transition to READY state (Emit SystemReadyEvent)
